    },
    {
      "role": "body",
      "text": "Population aging is shared by Japan and the United States, but national averages can conceal distinct regional patterns. We examine how population age structure relates to industrial composition and age-selective domestic migration, distinguishing differences between countries from variation within them.",
      "css_pt": 24,
      "x": 102.046875,
      "y": 684,
      "width": 956.21875,
      "height": 249.5625,
      "right": 1058.265625,
      "bottom": 933.5625
    },
    {
      "role": "caption",
      "text": "Historical estimates: residents aged 65+ as a share of the all-age population.",
      "css_pt": 20.000025,
      "x": 102.046875,
      "y": 2372.640625,
      "width": 956.21875,
      "height": 66.65625,
      "right": 1058.265625,
      "bottom": 2439.296875
    },
