      "height": 36.796875,
      "right": 3076.515625,
      "bottom": 3977.34375
    },
    {
      "role": "limitations-body",
      "text": "Associations are descriptive, not causal. Population dates, GDP reporting periods, service-sector definitions, and migration measures differ across countries. ACS estimates carry sampling uncertainty; Japanese migration rates use rounded population denominators. Two association snapshots do not establish patterns in every year, and one year's migration flows cannot fully explain accumulated population age structure.",
